WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.425
Your next pipeline starts with a drag.

00:00:03.704 --> 00:00:07.151
This is Duckpad: a visual workspace for

00:00:07.245 --> 00:00:09.667
turning data into answers.

00:00:09.853 --> 00:00:12.741
Drag in a step, connect your sources, and

00:00:12.881 --> 00:00:16.561
shape your data with simple controls or SQL.

00:00:16.655 --> 00:00:17.679
Need a hand?

00:00:17.819 --> 00:00:20.568
Ask the AI assistant about your flow.

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:23.735
It reads your project, explains the logic,

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:26.065
and can make changes you can review and

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.183
undo.

00:00:27.276 --> 00:00:30.444
Keep quality checks beside your SQL.

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:33.798
Run data tests, inspect failing rows, and

00:00:34.031 --> 00:00:36.220
surface useful messages right where you

00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:36.965
work.

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:39.947
Explore the result, then trace a value back

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.717
to the data behind it.

00:00:41.903 --> 00:00:44.419
Every change is versioned with Git, so you

00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:47.680
can compare, branch, and keep moving.

00:00:47.773 --> 00:00:50.195
From a first connection to a result you

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:51.593
understand.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.361
Duckpad. See the flow. Trust the result.
